    "id": "overlap-pilot3",
    "language": "Okay. So thinking about the overlap situation in which a teammate has the ball centrally, and you make a wide run to sort of stretch the opposition defense, and, uh, attract attention towards yourself to either, you know, burst past that player or give it back to your teammate who is now open. Uh, I'm gonna start the simulation[0] and run beyond my teammate. He's going[1] to see me in space[2] and give me a wide pass. And I think at this point, because of where my teammate's given me the ball, you can sort of tell that he's attracted the attention of this defender, uh, and this defender is now [3]much closer to me, um, than he is to my teammate. In a situation like this, it's sort of 50-50 about whether I want to give it back to my teammate or whether I want to have a, a run straight through on goal. I think, um, for the sake of this, because it seems like we're a little bit f- further away from goal, I'm going to receive it and[4] give it straight back to my teammate, uh, with a safe[5] pass, and then burst into space again. [6]Um, and at this point, it's up to the opposition defender to either track me or track my teammate. Either my teammate has lots of space to burst into, or, um, the oppo- I've got lots of space to burst into if I receive the ball back. Um, so I'm just gonna...",
